PianoInput is new code for UniXNU-piano (BSD-2-Clause-Patent, LICENSE) around one vendored class. What it takes from other work,
and from where:

macOS-DroidVM (github.com/Droid-VM/macOS-DroidVM; local archive droidvm-build/macOS-DroidVM, branch el1/native-variant
11ac316b789d81fc9f734e15645456f536c05141, read only), BSD-2-Clause-Patent (SPDX header of the file):
  overlay/kext/DroidVMInput/DroidVMInput.cpp (sha256 f05d9d9912b1ae5b57000dcc49f6a4539410e5212c34b31aa4270e31cfac8afc)
    Taken: the class DroidVMHIDDevice as PianoHIDDevice (PianoInput.cpp): an IOHIDDevice subclass with the same overrides
    (newReportDescriptor, newTransportString, newManufacturerString, newProductString, newVendorIDNumber, newProductIDNumber,
    newLocationIDNumber, newPrimaryUsagePageNumber, newPrimaryUsageNumber), set up under the driver's own service the same way
    (OSTypeAlloc, init, attach, start), reports through handleReport from a polling kernel thread, and describe()'s bring-up log
    of who is attached to the device's IOHIDInterface (and the user clients of its event service).
    Changed: what each device says comes from HidReports.h's DeviceInfo table (one row now: the buttons); transport "SPMI";
    the location ID; Built-In set on the buttons; a publish notification logs IOHIDEventDriver attaching.
    Removed: the virtio-input transport and queues, the keyboard/mouse/tablet/touch kinds, the Apple multitouch protocol
    (getReport/setReport feature reports, path frames, DefaultMultitouchProperties, displayUUID): the touch step takes those
    from the same file. Not taken at all: hidToLinux (a table from Linux's drivers/hid/usbhid/usbkbd.c) and the QEMU report
    descriptors.
  overlay/kext/DroidVMInput.json (sha256 a9f25963fb0b17376ccd27a1cef6cc864d383789afc137d000bcaf06327a9843)
    The shape of tooling/k27/kext/PianoInput.json: com.apple.iokit.IOHIDFamily 2.0.0 as a library, the codeless IOHIDEventDriver
    personality on IOHIDInterface (probe score 3000; PianoInput's own VendorID/ProductID pair), and the vtable check (IOHIDDevice,
    334 slots, slot 16 ignored).
  The IOKit/hid headers are not copied: tooling/k27/build-native-piano-input.sh includes the k27 tree's out/x12377/inc-hid (the
  headers DroidVMInput was built with), out/x12377/inc-gfx and out/x12377/storage-abi/include (TargetConditionals.h), read only.

UniXNU-piano (this repository), BSD-2-Clause-Patent:
  package/PianoDwc3/PianoDwc3.cpp at 7860af438e035b3a5035b243b84132bb9854a59c: the SPMI arbiter v7 reads (spmiApid, spmiRead:
  version and count check, APID map, the EE 0 owner preferred, the observer channel's one-byte read) and the MMIO helpers (rd32,
  wr32, mapRegion), re-expressed in SpmiObserver.h over an Io so tests/buttons_host.cpp runs them on a model.
  patches/k27/0057: the arbiter's window layout as its comment states it.

piano-uefi (unixnu-research/piano-uefi, branch unixnu 31545f9392d5f5c2acae14cec2fa3a0aa1de51d4)
  uefi/pianoPkg/Library/KeypadDeviceLib/KeypadDeviceLib.c (BSD-2-Clause; sha256 2a5deaa1321d570b93e14d44273cdc50e61670d18e3ae5e26af18c322fba5586):
  facts only: the key registers measured on this tablet (PON PPID 0x013 register 0x10 bits 7 and 6; GPIO PPID 0x18D register
  0x10 bit 0, active low) and the owner check. Its key state machine (from Mu-Silicium's Samsung a7 KeypadDeviceLib) is not used.

UniXNU-Odin3 (unixnu-research/UniXNU-Odin3, main 6d58c09d1529fb22dba8e3d6f74d8d4c7f9f8306) modules/Pagani/drivers/PaganiInput,
BSD-2-Clause-Patent: Buttons.h (sha256 5779464dc110d411679f8ff2af9531b7222f2715489c355d8eb7f6d6393e561a) and Reports.h
(sha256 2c3eec41d9108b7741ce66f3fe681f8794bc5913ba1eb41541d31c9fe65bbf31): the design of a polled buttons device (a consumer
report of Power, Volume Increment and Volume Decrement; a 32 ms debounce in which an unreadable sample counts as all keys up).
Re-implemented in Buttons.h and HidReports.h; its key polarities are the 13T's, not piano's.

Not read and not used: GPL code. piano-uefi selector/keys.c and Project-SunUEFI PianoKeys.c (GPL-2.0-only), and Linux's PON,
pwrkey and SPMI arbiter drivers (GPL-2.0). The register facts come from the BSD sources above and from
droidvm-build/piano-patches/touch-native-plan.md section 3; the report descriptor from the HID 1.11 specification and the HID
Usage Tables (consumer page 0x0C).
